<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Dedan</h1><p class="st-meta">700 BCE – 500 BCE (approx.) · capital Dedan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An oasis kingdom at al-Ula in the Hejaz, a key stop on the incense road and precursor of the Lihyanite kings.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dedan-state">Dedan</a>, the ancient name of the oasis at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alula">al-Ula</a>, is mentioned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a> as a trading people. A local monarchy is attested in Dadanitic inscriptions from around the 7th century BCE. The oasis grew rich supplying water and provisions to caravans moving between south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kings of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dedan-state">Dedan</a> are known by name from short inscriptions, and the town had sanctuaries of the god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhu-ghabat">Dhu Ghabat</a>. In the mid-6th century BCE the Babylonian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabonidus">Nabonidus</a> campaigned in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hejaz">Hejaz</a> and listed Dedan among the oases he took while residing at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tayma">Tayma</a>. A colony of Minaean merchants from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-main">Kingdom of Ma'in</a> was later based there.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the Babylonian interlude the oasis came under the Lihyanite dynasty, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-lihyan">Kingdom of Lihyan</a> ruled from the same site. The ruins at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-khuraybah">al-Khuraybah</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alula">al-Ula</a>, with their temple and lion tombs, are now excavated.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 700 BCE – 500 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Arabia and the Gulf</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:45.77%;width:3.98%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>700 BCE – 500 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dedan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Arabian polytheism (Dhu Ghabat)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dadanitic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dedan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-600&amp;focus=kingdom-of-dedan" aria-label="Kingdom of Dedan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5680 1201 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Dedan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6000 1457L6000 1457"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6000 1457h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6000 1457h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6000 1457h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dedan. <a href="/atlas?year=-600&amp;focus=kingdom-of-dedan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
